{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ראה אנכי", :translit "re'eh anokhi", :gloss "See, I"} {:he "ראה", :translit "re'eh", :gloss "See"} {:he "לכ\"א ואחד", :translit "le'khol echad va'echad", :gloss "to each and every one"} {:he "אנכי", :translit "anokhi", :gloss "I"} {:he "לפניכם", :translit "lifneikhem", :gloss "before you"} {:he "לכם", :translit "lakhem", :gloss "to you"} {:he "אתה תומיך גורלי", :translit "atah tomeikh gorali", :gloss "You uphold my lot"} {:he "בחיים", :translit "ba'chayim", :gloss "in life"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Singular vs. plural shift: 're'eh' is singular, 'lifneikhem' is plural."} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: 'anokhi' links verse here to first word of the Decalogue."} {:kind :other, :note "Sequential reading: preceding verse ends with 'lakhem,' this verse continues as direct address."}], :frame {:text "Moses taught Torah in a sequence: he reviewed each chapter to Aaron alone, then Aaron's sons entered and he repeated it, then the elders entered, then all Israel — as described at Eruvin 54b. The phrase 'anokhi' opening the Decalogue at Exodus 20:2 anchors all commandments, per the tradition that the Decalogue encompasses all 613 commandments. The individual 're'eh' addressed to each Israelite reflects that every person is obligated individually. The practice of covering lots when dividing portions parallels Moses' instruction to Israel here to see and choose the blessing rather than having it hidden. The verse 'atah tomeikh gorali' is Psalms 16:5, applied here as Israel asking God to support their hand in choosing the good portion.", :sources ["Eruvin 54b" "Exodus 20:2" "Psalms 16:5"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Singular vs. plural shift: 're'eh' is singular, 'lifneikhem' is plural.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: 'anokhi' links verse here to first word of the Decalogue.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Sequential reading: preceding verse ends with 'lakhem,' this verse continues as direct address.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:36:03.751322488Z", :model "glm-5.2"}